  "term": "idealization",
  "definition": "In this historical aesthetic sense, idealization is the way facts or truths are taken up and shaped into an ideal form. It involves building on qualities already present in what is being considered, while carrying forward its valued features, such as beauty or moral worth, and leaving out what seems discordant.",
